\h Proverbs
\toc1 Proverbs
\toc2 Proverbs
\toc3 Prv.
\mt1 Proverbs
\is1 Introduction
\ip This collection of \bk Proverbs\bk*, is one way of teaching so that godly people have good examples of sensible life principles. Most of these sayings concern a person's lifestyle and internal values. Perhaps the most critical proverb included in here is: “The first step towards being wise is to strive to obey Yahweh” (1:7; 9:10). The sayings illustrate the good results that can come from following wise paths and not that of stupidity, as the path of wicked people is like deep darkness (4:19), and in contrast, the path of those who do what is right, is like a bright light (v18).
\ip These proverbs are a collection of useful sayings that help to impart godly wisdom to the reader.
\iot Main components of this collection
\io1 Praising wisdom \ior 1:1–9:18\ior*
\io1 Shelomoh's (Solomon's) sayings \ior 10:1–29:27\ior*
\io1 Agur's sayings \ior 30:1-33\ior*
\io1 Various other proverbs \ior 31:1-31\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
